orkspace lifecycle, or archive generation is security-sensitive and should be researched explicitly | Required before finalizing provider + checkpoint modules |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/tech-design.md:350:### Q7. What exact persistence grain should capture environment events and checkpoint outcomes before the full canonical archive and derived-view work lands in the follow-on Feature 5 epic?\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/tech-design.md:353:not invent the full archive early.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/tech-design.md:362:  user-facing archive surface\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/tech-design.md:365:without pre-solving the full archive taxonomy.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/tech-design.md:681:| Full canonical archive entry taxonomy for environment/runtime events | AC-6, tech arch | Belongs to the archive follow-on slice | Feature 5 |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:6:process archive, turn derivation, and non-summarizing structural derived views.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:13:| Reviewers | Validate that archive work follows the core platform architecture |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:19:- Epic: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md`\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:20:- Test plan: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md`\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:26:surfaces, but the archive domain is coherent enough for one index document.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:30:Epic 7 is implementation-ready. It is scoped to canonical finalized archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:38:| Current `processHistoryItems` vocabulary differs from canonical archive taxonomy | Baseline, Tech Design Question 2 | Design adds new `archiveEntries` while bridging current history for compatibility. No historical migration/backfill is included. | Resolved - clarified |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:40:| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:45:archive finalization policy, read orchestration, turn derivation, and derived\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:53:| 1 | What durable schema stores archive entries, sequence numbers, related references, and idempotency keys? | Add `archiveEntries` with `projectId`, `processId`, `entryKind`, `sequence`, `finalizationKey`, `sourceObjectId`, body fields, related ids, status, and timestamps. Convex assigns sequence inside an append mutation and enforces `finalizationKey` idempotency per process. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:54:| 2 | What compatibility mapping bridges `processHistoryItems` and live updates, and is migration/backfill in scope? | Add compatibility helpers that map new finalized archive entries to existing process-history surfaces where needed. Existing `processHistoryItems` remain the legacy presentation read model. No historical migration/backfill is in scope for Epic 7. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:55:| 3 | What finalization boundary determines when entries are archived? | `ArchiveFinalizationService` is called only from completion points: accepted user responses, completed model/runtime objects, completed script emissions, finalized tool calls/results, and process events. Raw live deltas and interrupted partial objects never call append. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:56:| 4 | What derivation rules group archive entries into turns? | Turn derivation is deterministic over ordered archive entries. A `user_message` starts a new turn; following model/reasoning/script/tool/process entries attach to the active turn until the next `user_message`. Tool call/result correlation keeps paired tool entries in the same turn. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:57:| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:58:| 6 | What minimal derived-view representation should Epic 7 implement? | Implement structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` views with source turn/archive ids, optional labels, and status metadata. No model-generated summaries or summarization prompts. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:60:| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:61:| 9 | What idempotency strategy prevents duplicate archive entries? | `appendArchiveEntry` checks `processId + finalizationKey`. A replay returns the existing entry or no-ops. Sequence assignment happens only on first append. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:70:archive the PRD requires for long-horizon context management.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:72:Epic 7 introduces canonical archive truth without tearing out the live surface.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:74:UI state. Separately, completed process objects are finalized into archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:80:archive entries. A derived turn or chunk candidate can be rebuilt from the\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:81:archive. If derivation fails, the archive remains readable. That property is\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:96:| Processes | Core architecture | Finalization points and archive read access live under one project/process |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:98:| Projects | Core architecture | Project/process access gates archive reads |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:99:| Artifacts | Core architecture | Provides related artifact-version context during archive reads |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:100:| Sources | Core architecture + Epic 6 | Provides related source provenance context during archive reads |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:101:| Client | Core architecture | Adds process-surface entry points for archive, turn, and structural-view reads |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:114:    API[Fastify archive routes]\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:115:    UI[Client process/archive UI]\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:130:normalizes the finalized object into canonical archive entry shape and asks\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:133:The read path is broader. Fastify routes call `ArchiveReadService` for archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:135:structural views. These services read durable archive data and enrich related\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:137:entry or view rather than hiding the archive.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:143:| Add new `archiveEntries` instead of replacing `processHistoryItems` | Current history is presentation-oriented and already used by live process surfaces | Epic 7 can preserve archive truth without destabilizing current UI |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:146:| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:157:├── archiveEntries.ts                         # NEW: append/read canonical archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:158:├── archiveTurns.ts                           # NEW: cached derived turn records\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:160:└── schema.ts                                 # MODIFIED: archive tables and indexes\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:163:├── archive.ts                                # NEW: archive/turn/derived-view contracts and route builders\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:164:├── process-work-surface.ts                   # MODIFIED: optional archive entry points/actions in process surface contract\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:168:└── archive.ts                                # NEW: Fastify route schemas for archive APIs\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:171:└── archive.ts                                # NEW: authenticated archive/turn/derived-view routes\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:173:apps/platform/server/services/archive/\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:174:├── archive-finalization.service.ts           # NEW: finalized-object to archive-entry mapping\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:175:├── archive-read.service.ts                   # NEW: archive read/enrichment/degraded-state orchestration\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:177:├── derived-archive-view.service.ts           # NEW: structural view creation/read/refresh\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:178:└── process-history-compat.service.ts         # NEW: bridge archive entries to existing history surface when needed\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:181:└── platform-store.ts                         # MODIFIED: archive append/read/projection methods\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:185:├── process-response.service.ts               # MODIFIED: archive accepted user responses\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:189:├── archive-section.ts                        # NEW: process archive read surface\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:190:├── archive-turns-section.ts                  # NEW: derived turn surface\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:191:└── derived-archive-views-section.ts          # NEW: structural derived-view surface\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:194:└── bootstrap.ts                              # MODIFIED: route archive actions to process/archive surfaces\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:197:├── fixtures/archive.ts                       # NEW: archive/turn/v