s not affect canonical archive entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:333:The array fields in `archiveTurns` and `derivedArchiveViews` are intentionally\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:336:at the archive-entry and turn level rather than trying to persist one giant\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:341:Shared contracts live in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts`.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:354:  archiveEntryId: string;\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:382:  archiveEntryIds: string[];\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:408:| Get process archive | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive` | `ArchiveReadService.getArchive` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:409:| Get process turns | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/turns` | `TurnDerivationService.getTurns` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:410:| Get derived archive views | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:411:| Refresh derived archive views | POST | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views/refresh` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.refreshViews` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:414:enforce project/process access before archive services run.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:418:`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts` should define these route schemas:\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:420:- archive page query: `cursor?: string | null`, `limit?: number`\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:428:| `GET /archive` | `ArchivePage` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:429:| `GET /archive/turns` | `{ turns, page }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:430:| `GET /archive/derived-views` | `{ views }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:431:| `POST /archive/derived-views/refresh` | `{ views, refreshStatus }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `409`, `422` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:441:| 409 | `ARCHIVE_DERIVATION_CONFLICT` | Derived-view refresh cannot safely reconcile with current archive state |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:566:Trusted callers supply already-finalized archive-entry payloads to the durable\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:575:    participant X as Convex archiveEntries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:589:`process-live.ts`. Those live messages are not archive writes. Only completed\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:604:This flow covers AC-3.1 through AC-3.4. The user reads archive entries through\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:608:returns archive response rows for the client surface to render.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:613:canonical `archiveEntries` row unless the row itself was originally persisted\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:618:This flow covers AC-4.1 through AC-4.4. Turn derivation reads archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:630:  5. Degraded related context degrades the turn, not the archive entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:633:or explicit derived-view refresh, not on every archive append. Rebuild upserts by\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:651:ids. Building on the Flow 3 archive read surface, read services enrich when\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:660:the artifact/source lookup-failure degradation semantics: the archive entry\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:672:- archive entries: default 100, max 200\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:676:A derived-view read or rebuild failure does not block archive reads. Routes\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:677:return degraded view state for derived failures and keep archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:684:| 0 | Foundation | Contracts, Convex schema, fixtures, error codes, compatibility mapping skeletons | All support | Relevant sections: API Contracts, Data Model. Non-TC: archive contract vocabulary and finalized-only schema test |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:686:| 2 | Finalization boundary | Completion hooks, live/archive separation, retry idempotency | AC-2.x | Relevant sections: Flow 2, Service Interfaces. Non-TC: live-history separation, compatibility mapping decision |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:687:| 3 | Archive read/reopen | Routes, access controls, empty state, bounded page contract, environment-loss reads, degraded-entry display | AC-3.x | Relevant sections: Flow 3, Route Validation. Non-TC: invalid archive request handling |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:706:| Historical migration/backfill from `processHistoryItems` | A7 | Epic 7 starts forward canonical archive and 