 archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:55:that live state model separate from canonical archive writes. A current object\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:57:appended to the canonical archive.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:65:This epic delivers the first canonical archive and derived-view slice:\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:67:- Full-fidelity process archive entries at finalized low-level grain\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:68:- Canonical archive entry taxonomy from the platform PRD\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:70:- Read surfaces for process archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:71:- Turn derivation from archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:73:- Provenance from derived turns/views back to archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:74:- Bounded degraded states when archive reads or derivation reads partially fail\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:76:- Reopen behavior for archive, turn, and derived-view reads\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:87:- Generic transcript export product beyond the archive/derived-view contracts\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:94:| A2 | Existing process history remains a process work-surface read model | Validated | Platform | Epic 7 may bridge from current history, but canonical archive uses the PRD entry taxonomy |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:95:| A3 | Live process updates continue to use typed current-object upserts | Validated | Platform | Epic 7 adds finalization-to-archive behavior rather than replacing live transport |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-der