pic.md:130:- **TC-1.1c: Process event archived**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:133:  - Then: A `process_event` archive entry is appended for that process\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:135:**AC-1.2:** The canonical archive supports the PRD entry taxonomy.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:137:- **TC-1.2a: Required archive entry kinds accepted**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:138:  - Given: The platform appends finalized archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:140:  - Then: The archive accepts `user_message`, `model_message`, `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, and `process_event`\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:141:- **TC-1.2b: Unsupported archive entry kind rejected**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:142:  - Given: A caller attempts to append an unsupported archive entry kind\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:144:  - Then: The platform rejects the entry and does not append a partial archive record\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:148:- **TC-1.3a: Process archive entries read in stable order**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:149:  - Given: Multiple archive entries exist for one process\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:150:  - When: The archive is read in ascending order\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:153:  - Given: Multiple archive entries have the same timestamp\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:154:  - When: The archive is read\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:160:  - Given: An archive entry relates to an artifact version or artifact event\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:161:  - When: The archive entry is read\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:165:  - When: The archive entry is read\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:166:  - Then: The archive entry remains visible with bounded degraded related-context metadata\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:170:The browser may receive live updates while work is active. The archive receives\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:171:only completed entries. The live current-object model and canonical archive do\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:177:4. The platform appends only completed objects to the archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:178:5. Interrupted partial objects remain outside canonical archive truth\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:182:**AC-2.1:** Raw streaming deltas are not stored as canonical archive entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:184:- **TC-2.1a: Streaming delta excluded from archive**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:186:  - When: The process archive is read\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:187:  - Then: Raw deltas do not appear as archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:189:**AC-2.2:** Interrupted partial objects are not archived as finalized entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:193:  - When: The process archive is read\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:194:  - Then: The interrupted partial object is not returned as a finalized archive entry\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:197:  - When: The process archive is read\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:198:  - Then: The incomplete tool result is not returned as a finalized archive entry\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:202:- **TC-2.3a: Completed live object archived once**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:205:  - Then: The platform appends one finalized archive entry for that object\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:206:- **TC-2.3b: Replayed completion does not duplicate archive entry**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:207:  - Given: A completion event is retried for an already-archived object\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:208:  - When: The archive append path processes the retry\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:214:pause, or environment loss. Archive reads use durable archive state, not active\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:217:1. User opens a process with archived history\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:218:2. System reads the canonical archive for that process\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:221:5. System restores the same canonical archive view\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:225:**AC-3.1:** The user can read finalized archive entries for one process.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:228:  - Given: A process has finalized archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:229:  - When: User opens the archive read surface for that process\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:231:- **TC-3.1b: Empty archive state visible**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:232:  - Given: A process has no archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:233:  - When: User opens the archive read surface\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:234:  - Then: The platform shows an empty archive state\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:236:**AC-3.2:** Reopening a process restores archive entries from durable state.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:239:  - Given: A process has finalized archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:241:  - Then: The archive entries are restored from durable state\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:243:  - Given: A process environment was discarded after entries were archived\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:244:  - When: User opens the process archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:245:  - Then: The archived entries remain available\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:249:- **TC-3.3a: Unauthorized archive read blocked**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:251:  - When: User requests a process archive from that project\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:252:  - Then: The platform rejects the request and does not leak archive content\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:253:- **TC-3.3b: Missing process archive read returns not found**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:255:  - When: User requests the process archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:258:**AC-3.4:** One degraded archive entry does not hide healthy archive entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:261:  - Given: One archive entry has unresolved related context and other entries are healthy\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:262:  - When: User reads the archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:267:Turns are derived groupings over archive entries. The platform can show or\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:270:Turn derivation uses deterministic grouping inputs from the archive, such as\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:273:derivation over the same archive entries must return the same turn boundaries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:278:4. A later archive entry is appended\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:283:**AC-4.1:** The platform can derive turns from archived entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:285:- **TC-4.1a: Turns derived from archive**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:286:  - Given: A process has archive entries that form one or more interaction turns\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:288:  - Then: The platform returns turns derived from archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:289:- **TC-4.1b: Empty archive produces empty turn view**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:290:  - Given: A process has no archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:294:**AC-4.2:** Each derived turn references the archive entries it groups.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:296:- **TC-4.2a: Turn includes archive entry references**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:297:  - Given: A turn is derived from archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:299:  - Then: The turn includes references to the archive entries used to derive it\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:301:**AC-4.3:** Turn derivation does not mutate canonical archive entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:304:  - Given: A process has archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:306:  - Then: The canonical archive entries remain unchanged\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:320:more turns. It identifies boundaries, source turns, source archive entries, and\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:324:Derived views remain rebuildable from turns and archive entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:329:4. The derived view links back to the source turns and archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:330:5. Later derived views can be rebuilt without changing the archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:349:  - Then: The view identifies its source turn range and covered archive-entry\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:352:**AC-5.3:** Derived views preserve provenance back to turns and archive entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:358:- **TC-5.3b: Derived view can trace to archive entries**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:360:  - When: The source archive references are inspected\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:361:  - Then: The underlying archive entry references remain available\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:363:**AC-5.4:** Derived views do not replace or delete full-fidelity archive entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:367:  - When: User reads the canonical archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:368:  - Then: The full-fidelity archive entries remain available\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:370:**AC-5.5:** Derived-view generation can degrade without corrupting canonical archive state.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:372:- **TC-5.5a: Derived view failure leaves archive readable**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:374:  - When: User reads the canonical archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:375:  - Then: The archive remains readable and unchanged\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:379:  - Then: The platform returns a degraded derived-view state without hiding the canonical archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:387:2. The process emits finalized archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:390:4. User reads archive, turn, or derived-view surfaces\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:398:- **TC-6.1a: Artifact provenance visible from archive entry**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:399:  - Given: An archive entry relates to an artifact version\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:400:  - When: User reads the archive entry\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:405:- **TC-6.2a: Source provenance visible from archive entry**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:406:  - Given: An archive entry relates to a source that informed or received work\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:407:  - When: User reads the archive entry\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:410:**AC-6.3:** Missing related provenance does not hide archive truth.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:413:  - Given: An archive entry references source provenance that cannot be fully resolved\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:414:  - When: User reads the archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md: