/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/coverage.md:52:| Path 2.3 | Receive and keep a specific outstanding request visible in context | Story 3 | TC-3.2a, TC-5.2a |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/coverage.md:53:| Path 2.4 | Submit a valid response and see it appear in visible history in the same session | Story 3 | TC-3.6a |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/coverage.md:54:| Path 2.5 | Distinguish routine progress from attention-required moments while the request remains unresolved | Story 3 | TC-5.1a, TC-5.1b |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/coverage.md:56:| Path 3.2 | Follow distinct side work and its returned result or failure | Story 5 | TC-5.3a, TC-5.4a, TC-5.4b |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/02-start-and-resume.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The work surface must support substantial process conversation and active progress without flattening the experience into generic chat or forcing the user to reconstruct context from the shell alone.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/02-start-and-resume.md:31:- User-authored in-context responses\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/05-side-work-visibility.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The work surface must support substantial process conversation and active progress without flattening the experience into generic chat or forcing the user to reconstruct context from the shell alone.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/05-side-work-visibility.md:38:- Story 3 current-request and conversation behavior\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/05-side-work-visibility.md:46:- **TC-5.3a: Active side work shown distinctly**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/05-side-work-visibility.md:50:- **TC-5.3b: Multiple side-work items remain distinguishable**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/05-side-work-visibility.md:57:- **TC-5.4a: Completed side work shows returned result**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/05-side-work-visibility.md:61:- **TC-5.4b: Failed side work shows failure outcome**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/05-side-work-visibility.md:65:- **TC-5.4c: Parent-process change shown after side work outcome**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/05-side-work-visibility.md:110:- Story tests cover TC-5.3a through TC-5.4c\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/06-live-reconciliation-and-degradation.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The work surface must support substantial process conversation and active progress without flattening the experience into generic chat or forcing the user to reconstruct context from the shell alone.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:1:# Story 3: Conversation and Current Request\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:5:Keep process conversation, pinned current requests, and attention-required visibility in one surface while persisting valid user responses into durable history.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The work surface must support substantial process conversation and active progress without flattening the experience into generic chat or forcing the user to reconstruct context from the shell alone.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:18:Support multi-turn process conversation, keep unresolved current requests visible and distinct from routine progress, persist accepted user responses into history, and prevent false waiting or partial-submit states.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:26:- Distinction between routine progress and attention-required current requests\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:27:- Durable history for accepted user responses\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:28:- Rejection of invalid responses without partial visible history\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:29:- Same-session state updates after successful response submission\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:46:**AC-3.1:** During process stages that support discussion or clarification, the work surface supports multi-turn back-and-forth between the user and the process.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:57:**AC-3.2:** When the process is waiting on a specific question, decision, or clarification, the outstanding request remains visible until it is addressed or superseded.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:63:- **TC-3.2b: Outstanding request clears or changes after response**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:66:  - Then: The outstanding request clears or is replaced by the new current request\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:68:**AC-3.3:** A submitted user response becomes part of durable process history for that process and remains visible when the user reloads or returns later.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:70:- **TC-3.3a: Submitted response appears in process history**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:71:  - Given: User submits a response in a process work surface\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:73:  - Then: The response appears in that process's visible history\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:75:  - Given: User previously submitted a response in a process\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:77:  - Then: The response still appears in that process's visible history\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:79:**AC-3.4:** When the current process state does not accept a user response, the surface shows the current next action or blocking state rather than presenting the process as waiting for a reply.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:90:**AC-3.5:** An invalid process response is rejected without creating a new visible history item for that process.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:92:- **TC-3.5a: Empty response is rejected**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:93:  - Given: User is in a process stage that accepts a response\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:94:  - When: User submits an empty or invalid response\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:95:  - Then: The response is rejected and no new visible history item is created\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:96:- **TC-3.5b: Failed response submission does not create partial history**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:97:  - Given: User submits a response in a process stage that accepts a response\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:101:**AC-3.6:** After a successful process response submission, the submitted response and resulting process state update appear in the same session without requiring manual refresh.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:103:- **TC-3.6a: Successful response appears in visible history in same session**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:104:  - Given: User submits a valid response in a process stage that accepts a response\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:106:  - Then: The submitted response appears in visible history in the same session without requiring manual refresh\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:107:- **TC-3.6b: Resulting current request or process state updates in same session**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:108:  - Given: User submits a valid response in a process stage that accepts a response\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:114:- **TC-5.1a: Routine progress remains distinct from attention-required request**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:118:- **TC-5.1b: Attention-required item remains visible in mixed activity**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:119:  - Given: Process continues to report routine progress around a current request\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:125:- **TC-5.2a: Unresolved request stays visible**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:129:- **TC-5.2b: Resolved request no longer shown as unresolved**\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:136:This story owns response submission, unresolved current-request visibility, and the history semantics that distinguish routine progress from attention-required moments.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:142:| Submit process response | POST | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/responses` | Submits one in-context user response into the current process |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:148:| `clientRequestId` | string | yes | non-empty | Client-generated correlation identifier for this response submission |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:149:| `message` | string | yes | trimmed, non-empty | User response text submitted into the current process |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:155:| `accepted` | boolean | yes | `true` | Indicates the response was accepted into the process |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:156:| `historyItemId` | string | yes | non-empty | Visible history item identifier for the accepted response |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:157:| `process` | object | yes | present | Updated process state needed to keep the visible work surface coherent after the accepted response |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:158:| `currentRequest` | Current Process Request | no | present when unresolved | Updated unresolved request after the accepted response, when one remains |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:160:After a successful response submission, the accepted response appears in visible history in the same session. Remaining process-surface changes continue through live updates; if live updates are unavailable, the surface reloads the current durable process work-surface state automatically.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:166:| `user_message` | A visible user-authored process message or response |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:167:| `process_message` | A visible process-authored conversational message |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:201:| `422` | `INVALID_PROCESS_RESPONSE` | Submitted process response is missing or invalid |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:210:- Accepted user responses become durable visible history and survive reload/return\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:212:- Same-session updates cover both the new response and the resulting visible process state\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:213:- Story tests cover TC-3.1a through TC-3.6b and TC-5.1a through TC-5.2b\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The work surface must support substantial process conversation and active progress without flattening the experience into generic chat or forcing the user to reconstruct context from the shell alone.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/01-process-entry-and-bootstrap.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The work surface must support substantial process conversation and active progress without flattening the experience into generic chat or forcing the user to reconstruct context from the shell alone.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/01-process-entry-and-bootstrap.md:27:- Bootstrap visible history, current materials, and unresolved current request state together\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/01-process-entry-and-bootstrap.md:33:- In-context response submission\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/01-process-entry-and-bootstrap.md:140:Section envelopes keep a stable top-level response shape across `ready`, `empty`, and `error` states.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/01-process-entry-and-bootstrap.md:257:- First-load rendering shows process identity, phase, status, next action or blocker, history, materials, current request state, and side-work envelope state\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:64:- `smoke check response`: `OK`\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:146:4. `03-conversation-and-current-request`\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:156:- Story 3 depends on Story 2.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:157:- Story 4 depends on Story 3 in the published story pack, even though the design chunks are conceptually separable.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:170:| Convex visible history table + request projection | stub | Story 1 / Story 3 |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:172:| Response submission path | stub | Story 3 |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:272:- Story 3: `47`\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:560:   - conservative `currentRequest` projection is acceptable for Story 1 but should be revisited in Story 3\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/ep