t.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/sonnet-review.md:74:`processLiveUnavailableErrorFixture` uses `requestErrorSchema` with `status: 503`. The fixture is type-valid for `live.error`, but the naming and status imply an HTTP response even though the design treats live unavailability as a transport state, not an HTTP bootstrap failure.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/02-start-and-resume/cursor-review-round-2.md:10:- Observed that the page suite now covers successful start/resume, stale `PROCESS_ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE` responses, and resulting waiting/completed/failed action payload rendering.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/02-start-and-resume/cursor-review-prompt.md:20:- AC-2.5 same-session state update from action responses\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/02-start-and-resume/cursor-review-prompt.md:23:- whether Story 2 drifts into Story 3 scope\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/02-start-and-resume/cursor-review.md:7:- I did not find Story 3 response submission or Story 6 live transport behavior leaking into the production changes.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/02-start-and-resume/codex-fix-round-1-prompt.md:26:- do not implement Story 3 response submission\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/verification-bundle.md:28:- Story 1: route model, bootstrap response/envelope contracts, process route scaffolding, direct-route test helpers\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/verification-bundle.md:29:- Stories 2-3: start/resume/respond response contracts, live-update vocabulary, live reducer and fixtures\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/02-start-and-resume/codex-review-round-1.md:19:- The server action