d producing-process provenance labels in degraded artifact review responses instead of dropping them when content fetch/render fails.\\\",\\\"Added evidence for the Story 2 latest-version projection rule at the project-shell API layer and for multi-process version provenance at the artifact review layer.\\\",\\\"Confirmed pass-2 requirement alignment: AC-2.1 write-path flip, AC-2.2 version provenance visibility, and AC-2.3 latest-summary plus earlier-version reviewability obligations are implemented and covered by updated tests and passing gates.\\\"],\\\"findingsSurfaced\\\":[]},\\\"openQuestions\\\":[],\\\"specDeviations\\\":[],\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\":\\\"Proceed to verification against AC-2.1 through AC-2.3, with reviewer focus on multi-process checkpoint revision flow, latest-version shell projection, and earlier-version review provenance.\\\"}\"}}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/artifacts/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment/streams/005-self-review-batch.stdout.log:11:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"ready-for-verification\\\",\\\"planSummary\\\":\\\"Implemented Story 2’s checkpoint realignment so artifact identity remains project-scoped, later revisions append new artifact versions with explicit producing-process provenance, and shell/review reads resolve current version state from durable version history instead of artifact ownership metadata.\\\",\\\"changedFiles\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"convex/artifacts.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Removed artifact-row process ownership from checkpoint persistence so revising an existing project artifact keeps one stable artifact identity and writes a new version row instead.\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Aligned the in-memory platform store with Story 2 by deriving artifact summaries from latest version history and avoiding ownership-style rewrites during checkpoint persistence.\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"apps/platform/server/services/review/artifact-review.service.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Preserved producing-process display provenance when artifact review content loading degrades into an error state.\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"convex/artifacts.test.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Added durable-state coverage for multi-process revisions keeping one artifact identity while recording separate version provenance.\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Added server coverage proving project-shell artifact summaries resolve currentVersionLabel and updatedAt from the latest durable version.\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Strengthened artifact review assertions so producing-process provenance remains visible in normal and degraded responses.\\\"}],\\\"tests\\\":{\\\"added\\\":[],\\\"modified\\\":[\\\"convex/artifacts.test.ts\\\",\\\"tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts\\\",\\\"tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts\\\"],\\\"removed\\\":[],\\\"totalAfterStory\\\":558,\\\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\\\":2},\\\"gatesRun\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm exec vitest run convex/artifacts.test.ts tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts tests/integration/review-workspace.test.ts --environment node\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"fail\\\"},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"}],\\\"selfReview\\\":{\\\"findingsFixed\\\":[\\\"Removed the Convex artifact-row reassignment behavior that let later checkpoint revisions overwrite artifact ownership semantics.\\\",\\\"Aligned in-memory shell/material artifact summaries with latest artifact version history so later revisions stay current even when producedAt ordering differs from durable version creation order.\\\",\\\"Preserved producing-process provenance labels in degraded artifact review responses instead of dropping them when content fetch/render fails.\\\",\\\"Added evidence for the Story 2 latest-version projection rule at the project-shell API layer and for multi-process version provenance at the artifact review layer.\\\",\\\"Confirmed AC-2.1, AC-2.2, and AC-2.3 obligations are implemented and covered by updated tests plus passing story/epic gates.\\\"],\\\"findingsSurfaced\\\":[\\\"InMemoryPlatformStore still carries a synthetic artifact-version fallback for seeded test data that lack explicit version rows; that is a test-store compatibility shim, not the Convex production path changed by this story.\\\",\\\"ArtifactSummary’s TypeScript shape still tolerates legacy optional ownership fields for fixture compatibility even though the runtime schema/output strip them; broader cleanup of those compatibility fields is adjacent follow-up work, not required to satisfy Story 2.\\\"]},\\\"openQuestions\\\":[],\\\"specDeviations\\\":[],\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\":\\\"Proceed to verification against AC-2.1 through AC-2.3, and optionally queue a follow-up cleanup task for the remaining test-only compatibility shims around legacy artifact ownership fields.\\\"}\"}}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/test-plan.md:280:| TC-2.3a | `TC-2.3a hydration progress becomes visible through environment live updates` | Existing surface state + environment preparing update | Apply live message | Environment state becomes preparing |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/test-plan.md:281:| TC-2.3b | `TC-2.3b hydration failure becomes visible through environment live updates` | Accepted action state + failed environment update | Apply live message | Environment state becomes failed/unavailable |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/artifacts/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment/streams/012-verify.stdout.log:4:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '56,98p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment.md && printf '\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n' && sed -n '343,407p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design-client.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"**AC-2.2:** Version-level provenance identifies which process produced each artifact revision.\\n\\n- **TC-2.2a: Producing process recorded on version**\\n  - Given: A new artifact version is created\\n  - When: Version provenance is read later\\n  - Then: The producing process for that version is visible\\n- **TC-2.2b: Earlier version provenance remains readable**\\n  - Given: An artifact has versions produced by multiple processes\\n  - When: Earlier versions are reviewed\\n  - Then: Each earlier version still shows the process that produced it\\n\\n**AC-2.3:** Current artifact summaries resolve the latest version correctly after multi-process revision history.\\n\\n- **TC-2.3a: Latest version shown after later process revision**\\n  - Given: A later process created a new artifact version\\n  - When: Current artifact summaries are loaded\\n  - Then: The summaries show the latest current version label and update time\\n- **TC-2.3b: Earlier versions remain reviewable**\\n  - Given: An artifact has more than one version\\n  - When: The user opens artifact review\\n  - Then: Earlier versions remain available for selection and review\\n\\n### Technical Design\\n<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\nThis story owns the write-path flip from artifact-row ownership semantics to version-row provenance semantics.\\n\\n#### Endpoints Affected By Read Model\\n\\n| Operation | Method | Path | Description |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Get project shell | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project-level artifact state with project-scoped artifact identity and latest version summary |\\n| Get process work surface | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | Returns process-local current artifact materials and current outputs without implying artifact ownership |\\n| Get artifact review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns one artifact's version list and selected review state for that process context |\\n\\n#### Artifact Version Summary\\n\\n| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Description |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `versionId` | string | yes | non-empty | Stable artifact version identifier |\\n| `versionLabel` | string | yes | non-empty | User-visible version label |\\n| `createdAt` | timestamp | yes | ISO 8601 UTC | Version creation timestamp |\\n| `producedByProcessId` | string | yes | non-empty | Process that created this version |\\n| `producedByProcessDisplayLabel` | string | no | non-empty when present | User-facing producing-process label |\\n\\n---\\n- selected-version metadata and version-switcher rows expose\\n  `producedByProcessId` and `producedByProcessDisplayLabel` so the producing\\n  process remains visible in the review experience\\n\\n### `package-review-panel.ts`\\n\\nThis panel already renders:\\n\\n- package identity and type\\n- member nav\\n- selected-member subpanel\\n- export trigger\\n\\nEpic 5 keeps that structure and changes the interpretation:\\n\\n- selected member failure messages refer to unavailable pinned versions\\n- mixed-producer members are normal\\n- fully degraded published packages still remain targetable so reopen and\\n  provenance inspection remain possible\\n- exportability is still server-driven, but the client copy should explain\\n  \\\"One or more pinned members are unavailable\\\" rather than \\\"This package is not\\n  owned by the current process\\\"\\n\\n## Interface Definitions\\n\\n### Project Artifact Summary\\n\\n```ts\\nexport interface ArtifactSummary {\\n  artifactId: string;\\n  displayName: string;\\n  currentVersionLabel: string | null;\\n  updatedAt: string;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Review Version Contracts\\n\\n```ts\\nexport interface ArtifactVersionSummary {\\n  versionId: string;\\n  versionLabel: string;\\n  isCurrent: boolean;\\n  createdAt: string;\\n  producedByProcessId: string;\\n  producedByProcessDisplayLabel: string | null;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ArtifactVersionDetail extends ArtifactVersionSummary {\\n  contentKind: 'markdown' | 'unsupported';\\n  bodyStatus?: 'ready' | 'error';\\n  body?: string;\\n  bodyError?: ReviewTargetError;\\n  mermaidBlocks?: MermaidBlock[];\\n}\\n```\\n\\nClient consequences:\\n\\n- `version-switcher.ts` can keep its current listbox structure, but its row\\n  metadata should include the producing process display label, falling back to\\n  the id only when no display label can be resolved\\n- `artifact-review-panel.ts` should render the selected version's producing\\n  process display label beside the created timestamp, again falling back to the\\n  id only when needed\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/artifacts/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment/streams/012-verify.stdout.log:6:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff -- apps/platform/client/features/review/artifact-review-panel.ts apps/platform/client/features/review/version-switcher.ts tests/service/client/artifact-review-panel.test.ts tests/service/client/version-switcher.test.ts tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"diff --git a/apps/platform/client/features/review/artifact-review-panel.ts b/a