nt-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-verification-r2/sonnet-adversarial-review.md:395:| TC-2.3a | Hydration progress visible | `process-live.test.ts` (client) | SATISFIED |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-verification-r2/sonnet-adversarial-review.md:396:| TC-2.3b | Hydration failure visible | `process-live.test.ts` (client) | SATISFIED |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:1:# Story 2: Start or Resume with Environment Preparation\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:71:- **TC-2.3a: Hydration progress becomes visible**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:75:- **TC-2.3b: Hydration failure becomes visible**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-verification-r2/gpt54-xhigh-review.md:532:### TC-2.3a — SATISFIED\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-verification-r2/gpt54-xhigh-review.md:538:### TC-2.3b — SATISFIED\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-verification/sonnet-review.md:111:| TC-2.3a | Given: Preparation begun. When: Hydration in progress. Then: Environment shows hydration underway. | `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts` (environmentPreparingUpsertLiveFixture applied) | `process-environment.service.ts:196-283` executeHydration publishes preparing state via live hub | Client live test applies preparing upsert and verifies state transition. Server publishes through `processLiveHub.publish`. | **SATISFIED** |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-verification/sonnet-review.md:112:| TC-2.3b | Given: Recoverable hydration failure. When: Failure reported. Then: Environment shows failure without manual refresh. | `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts` (environmentFailedUpsertLiveFixture applied); `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts` | `process-environment.service.ts:253-283` catches hydration error, upserts `failed` state, publishes via live hub | Implementation catches hydration error, builds failed environment, publishes upsert. Client test confirms failed state applied. | **SATISFIED** |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review-round-3.md:1:# Story 2 Round 3 — Codex xhigh Verifier\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review-round-3.md:11:| AC-2.3 | TC-2.3a | SATISFIED | Preparation progress is returned immediately and later published live without refresh (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:21-23`, `57-64`); client reducer and websocket tests cover preparing visibility (`tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:88-106`, `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts:397-468`). |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review-round-3.md:12:| AC-2.3 | TC-2.3b | SATISFIED | Hydration failure is persisted as `failed` and published live without replacing the accepted action response (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:67-80`); failure visibility is covered in client and websocket tests (`tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:109-129`, `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts:474-547`). |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-2.md:1:# Story 2 Round-2 Compliance Review\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-2.md:65:- `TC-2.3a`: client test applies `environmentPreparingUpsertLiveFixture` and asserts `environment.state = preparing` in the store.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-2.md:66:- `TC-2.3b`: client test applies `environmentFailedUpsertLiveFixture` (renamed from the prior `environmentCheckpointFailureUpsertLiveFixture`) and asserts `state: 'failed'`, `blockedReason` non-null, `lastCheckpointResult: null`. The semantics shift is correct — preparation failure has no checkpoint result.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-2.md:140:Added four new tests: `TC-2.3a`, `TC-2.3b`, `TC-2.4a`, `TC-2.4b` — all new, all pass, all correctly test the live update reconciliation path.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-2.md:142:Renamed two prior tests: `TC-2.4a` (waiting transition) → \"waiting transition is reflected...\"; `TC-2.4b` (completed transition) → \"completed transition is reflected...\"; `TC-2.3a` (progress updates appear) → \"progress updates appear...\"; `TC-2.3b` (new history activity) → \"new history activity appears...\". These were TC labels inherited from Story 1 behavior. Removal of the Story-1 TC labels is correct — those tests remain valid but they covered different semantics. The new TC-2.3a through TC-2.4b tests now hold the Story-2 TC labels appropriately.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-2.md:158:**TF-3 (nonblocking):** The client tests for TC-2.3a, TC-2.3b, TC-2.4a, TC-2.4b are implemented at the `applyLiveProcessMessage` layer, testing the pure state function. This is correct and sufficient for the client contract. They do not require server integration to be valuable. When provider execution is added, server-side live-update tests should be added to verify the server produces these messages.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-2.md:180:**CG-3 (nonblocking):** `process-live-updates.test.ts` is not in the current diff. The test plan names it as a primary file for TC-2.3a, TC-2.3b, TC-2.4a, TC-2.4b at the server layer. The current tree covers those TCs only from the client perspective.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-2.md:240:**Observation 5 — `process-materials-section.test.ts` has 3 tests, test plan specifies 4:** The test plan specifies 4 tests for this file: TC-2.5a, TC-2.5b, TC-4.3a, plus one non-TC decided (\"mixed writable and read-only sources remain individually labeled\"). The round-2 bundle reports 3 passing tests. TC-4.3a (read-only source does not present a code-checkpoint path) is listed in the test plan but is a Story 4 AC, so its absence in the Story 2 implementation is expected. However the non-TC decided mixed-source label test is not present either. Minor gap, not a blocker for Story 2.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice4c-report.md:3:Slice 4c: Wire start/resume response fixtures to `preparingEnvironmentFixture` and add environment-panel assertions to the two Story 2 in-session tests (TC-2.1a/TC-2.5a and TC-2.1b/TC-2.5b).\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/03-controlled-execution-and-live-environment-state.md:40:- Story 2 environment preparation and hydration\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:4:- [High] AC-2.2 is not implemented for current outputs. Story 2 requires environment preparation to hydrate the process's current artifacts, current outputs, and current sources into the working copy (`stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:58-67`). The new working-set types only carry `artifactIds` and `sourceAttachmentIds` (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:63-71`), and `planHydrationWorkingSet()` copies only those two arrays (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/hydration-planner.ts:1-13`). The new Story 2 action tests only assert those two fields as well (`tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:956-1042`). Current outputs never enter the preparation path, so the implementation cannot satisfy AC-2.2 as written.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:6:- [High] AC-2.4 is violated because the accepted `start` / `resume` path still moves the process itself to `running` before readiness is confirmed. The underlying Convex mutations immediately call `transitionProcessToRunning()` for both actions (`convex/processes.ts:334-349`, `convex/processes.ts:702-726`), and the page renders `process.status` directly in the header (`apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts:101-105`). The new tests explicitly codify this by expecting `Running` while the environment panel still says `Preparing environment` (`tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:806-891`, `tests/service/client/process-work-surface-page.test.ts:1343-1396`). That contradicts Story 2's requirement that active running work begins only after readiness and that the surface does not falsely present the process as actively running after failed preparation (`stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:80-89`).\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:9:- The Story 2 implementation does not align with the chunk-2 server architecture. The design says `start` / `resume` should become thin wrappers over `ProcessEnvironmentService`, which then owns hydration planning, provider selection, and later lifecycle publication (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/tech-design-server.md:786-806`). The current tree skips that layer entirely: app assembly wires only `ProcessStartService` / `ProcessResumeService`, and the `services/processes/environment/` directory contains only the planner helper (`apps/platform/server/app.ts:110-121`, `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/hydration-planner.ts:1-13`). This is not just an internal refactor gap; it is the reason AC-2.3 and AC-2.4 are currently unmet.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:13:- `git diff 326d8c9cc4ac6455f70bc9a9fe9c5c9ab1b81579 -- **/*.test.* **/*.spec.*` shows Story 2 added meaningful client/server assertions, but the new coverage is concentrated on immediate action responses and fixture-driven reducer updates rather than a real accepted-action -> hydrate -> ready/failed lifecycle.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:16:- `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts` was not extended for Story 2. Its environment coverage is still a generic manual hub publication (`tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts:166-263`), so server-side TC-2.3 / TC-2.4 behavior remains unproven.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:20:- Story traceability regressed in the new test names. `tests/service/client/process-work-surface-page.test.ts:1343-1399` introduces `TC-2.6a/b/c`, but Story 2 has no TC-2.6 series. That makes the spec-to-test audit trail harder to trust.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:21:- Several newly relabeled client tests cover reducer behavior only, not end-to-end Story 2 behavior. For example, `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:131-188` labels TC-2.4 coverage without asserting any process-status transition sequencing from the server side.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:25:- Story 2 is not sufficient for AC-2.2 because current outputs are absent from the working-set contract and therefore cannot be hydrated.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:26:- Story 2 is not sufficient for AC-2.3 because there is no implemented provider-backed or server-driven lifecycle that can publish hydration progress or hydration failure after action acceptance.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:27:- Story 2 is not sufficient for AC-2.4 because the accepted path marks the process as `running` before readiness and the UI/tests intentionally present that as active running.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:30:- `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/tech-design-server.md` was widened in this diff with provider-selection policy text, but the corresponding provider/orchestrator architecture still is not present in code. That change may be valid future direction, but it does not describe delivered Story 2 behavior yet.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:31:- `tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts` and `tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts` were updated only to satisfy the expanded `PlatformStore` interface. Those changes are fine, but they do not add Story 2 confidence.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review.md:39:- The green gate is not sufficient to accept the story because the missing Story 2 behaviors above are masked by in-memory-store assertions and fixture-only live-update tests.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice6-report.md:1:# Slice 6 Implementation Report — Story 2 Hydration Planning Helper\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-review-sonnet.md:82:| TC-2.3a | SATISFIED | `process-live.test.ts`: \"TC-2.3a hydration progress becomes visible through environment live updates\" — `preparing` state received via live upsert |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-review-sonnet.md:83:| TC-2.3b | SATISFIED | `process-live.test.ts`: \"TC-2.3b hydration failure becomes visible through environment live updates\" — `failed` state with `blockedReason` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-review-sonnet.md:241:**Story 1 → Story 2:** `buildProcessSurfaceSummary()` accepts an `EnvironmentSummary` argument and correctly derives `controls` and `hasEnvironment` from both process and environment state. Story 2 uses this in `process-start.service.ts` and `process-resume.service.ts` — clean composition.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-review-sonnet.md:243:**Story 2 → Story 3:** `runHydrationAsync()` is called fire-and-forget from start/resume services. The hydration async path transitions to `ready` then publishes a live upsert. Story 3's live test sequence (`preparing → ready → running`) correctly traces this path.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/verification-bundle.md:1:# Story 2 Verification Bundle\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/verification-bundle.md:8:  `Story 2: Start or Resume with Environment Preparation`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/verification-bundle.md:21:  - `TC-2.3a`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/verification-bundle.md:22:  - `TC-2.3b`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/verification-bundle.md:139:  - passed on the current Story 2 tree\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with