`{artifactIds, sourceAttachmentIds}` plan in PlatformStore and does nothing else — no provider call, no working copy, no files written. The environment stays `preparing` forever. This is the residual risk the verification bundle flags. Two paths to clear it: (a) scope-adjust the AC to say \\\"builds a hydration plan\\\" instead of \\\"hydrates,\\\" or (b) stub a call through to `provider.hydrateEnvironment()` (~2 hours).\\n\\n**What is solid:**\\n- **AC-2.1 fully satisfied.** Start and resume enter `preparing` state in the same session, the response includes `environment`, the bootstrap reflects it durably. Two-call server test (action + GET) is stronger than typical.\\n- **AC-2.5 fully satisfied.** Sources render `Access: read only` / `Access: read write` at both client and server layers, with correct test coverage.\\n- **AC-2.3 and AC-2.4 satisfied at the client layer.** Live reconciliation of `preparing` → `failed`, `preparing` → `ready` → `running` sequences all tested correctly. The fixture rename (`environmentCheckpointFailureUpsertLiveFixture` → `environmentFailedUpsertLiveFixture`) is semantically correct.\\n\\n**Nonblocking warnings:**\\n- TC-2.6a/b/c are undeclared TCs — should be labeled as non-TC decided tests.\\n- `process-live-updates.test.ts` not extended for Story 2 (TC-2.3a/b server-side publication gap).\\n- `S2-TC-2.4b` label covers terminal process status, not in-flight preparation failure — mislabeled relative to the AC scenario.\\n- `WorkingSetPlan` vs. `HydrationPlan` schema divergence will constrain Story 3 design (missing fingerprint, display names, per-source accessMode/targetRef, outputs).\",\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-client.md:318:| TC-2.3a | prior version opens distinctly | `tests/service/client/version-switcher.test.ts` | click prior version from two-version list | new versionId becomes selection; body re-renders |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-client.md:319:| TC-2.3b | versions ordered newest to oldest | `tests/service/client/version-switcher.test.ts` | three versions | DOM order descending by createdAt |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review-round-2.md:5:- Blocking: the process still enters `running` before readiness. The shared Convex transition helper immediately patches `status: 'running'` (`convex/processes.ts:702-727`), and the Story 2 services then overlay `environment.state = preparing` on top of that (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-start.service.ts:33-67`, `apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-resume.service.ts:33-68`). AC-2.4 says active running begins only after the required working set is ready or a recoverable failure is shown.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review-round-2.md:9:- The implementation does not match the Story 2 server architecture. The tech design expects `process-environment.service.ts`, `environment-orchestrator.ts`, and provider-adapter wiring to own accepted-action vs later-hydration work, but `createApp()` still wires only the legacy process services and no environment subsystem (`apps/platform/server/app.ts:78-121`). In the current tree, `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/` contains only `hydration-planner.ts`.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review-round-2.md:13:- `git diff 326d8c9cc4ac6455f70bc9a9fe9c5c9ab1b81579 -- **/*.test.* **/*.spec.*` shows Story 2 changes concentrated in client page/live/materials tests and server action/bootstrap tests. No server live-update test was added for action-driven hydration progress or failure.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/codex-review-round-2.md:22:- Traceability drift: new client tests use `TC-2.6a/b/c` labels even though Story 2 acceptance criteria stop at `TC-2.5b`. That makes auditability noisier than it needs to be.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/verification-bundle-round-2.md:1:# Story 2 Verification Bundle — Round 2\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/verification-bundle-round-2.md:8:  `Story 2: Start or Resume with Environment Preparation`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/verification-bundle-round-2.md:21:  - `TC-2.3a`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/verification-bundle-round-2.md:22:  - `TC-2.3b`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/verification-bundle-round-2.md:128:  working-copy hydration execution. Reviewers should decide whether Story 2 as\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/verification-bundle-round-2.md:136:Does the current Story 2 tree now satisfy AC-2.2 through AC-2.4 strongly enough\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice5-report.md:1:# Slice 5 — Story 2 Live/Store Explicit TC Coverage\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice5-report.md:5:Make four Story 2 test criteria explicit in the live/store test suite:\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice5-report.md:7:- **TC-2.3a** hydration progress becomes visible through environment live updates\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice5-report.md:8:- **TC-2.3b** hydration failure becomes visible through environment live updates\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice5-report.md:13:1. Rename two existing unlabeled env tests to carry the correct TC-2.3a / TC-2.3b identifiers.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice5-report.md:14:2. Strip incorrect TC-2.3a/b and TC-2.4a/b labels from history and process-state tests that had been mislabeled in a previous pass.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice5-report.md:21:  - Renamed `'applies environment upserts as first-class current-object state'` → `'TC-2.3a hydration progress becomes visible through environment live updates'`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice5-report.md:22:  - Renamed `'preserves checkpoint-result visibility on environment failure updates'` → `'TC-2.3b hydration failure becomes visible through environment live updates'`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice5-report.md:23:  - Removed misapplied `TC-2.3a` / `TC-2.3b` prefixes from history-ordering tests\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:10:## Orchestrator failure mode — Story 2 \"verify-round churn from under-configured fixer + unchecked fix spillover\" (2026-04-23 ~16:50Z)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:12:**The failure mode.** Story 2 accumulated **6 verify rounds + 5 quick-fixes + 2 `story-continue`s** before the final-round Story 2 findings converged on zero. Story 0 needed 4 rounds, Story 1 needed 3 rounds, Story 2 reached 6 and was still compounding — not because verifiers were nitpicking, but because every fix pass **either missed part of the fix's spillover or introduced a new defect the next round caught**.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:14:**Concrete chain on Story 2:**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:24:1. **Quick-fixer under-configured for the work it was doing.** Config had `quick_fixer` at `gpt-5.4 / medium` — the model-tier assumption is that quick-fixes are one-line corrections (typo, rename, dead-code removal). The Story 2 fixes routed through quick-fix were non-trivial integrations (three-surface scoping change, Convex mutation rewrite, server/client contract shape change). Medium reasoning effort + no reading journey → fixer focused narrowly on the flagged evidence and missed adjacent call sites that needed the same treatment. **Mitigation applied at 16:55Z: bumped `quick_fixer.reasoning_effort` from `medium` → `xhigh` in `impl-run.config.json` for the remainder of the run.**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:38:- **The config-schema defaults should probably set `quick_fixer.reasoning_effort` to `high` (not `medium`)** to absorb the typical case where orchestrators route non-trivial work through quick-fix because it's quicker than re-loading the reading journey. This is a low-cost change that would have prevented several of the Story 2 rounds.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:42:**Accepted for now / not reopening.** Story 2 round 6 is in flight. Letting it finish. Regardless of outcome, Story 2 acceptance stands or gets one more bounded correction — not another full `story-implement` reset. The lessons above are booked for Stories 3-6.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:53:2. **Treated self-review's `specDeviations` as disclosure rather than a routing signal.** When a self-review pass declares a spec deviation, that is the implementor admitting it did not finish the integration. The correct response is `story-continue` with a bounded follow-up, not \"noted.\" The skill's fix-routing doc is explicit: declared deviations and blocking verifier findings route to same-session follow-up.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:54:3. **Treated convergent verifier findings as debatable opinions.** Two fresh verifiers independently flagging the same integration gap with `blocking: true` is the strongest signal the CLI produces. Overriding it requires tech-design evidence against the verifiers' interpretation, not scope-argument rationalization.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:71:- Story 2 was dispatched at ~10:55Z and stopped at ~11:05Z before self-review. Story 2 partial edits rolled back (git checkout HEAD + rm of untracked + rm of `artifacts/02-.../`). Working tree back to Story 1 commit state.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:105:| 20 | Codex subprocess hangs for 40+ min (2 instances observed) with ~1s CPU, no output progression | **OPEN (intermittent, repeat offender)** | At 2026-04-23 ~15:37Z, Story 2 `story-continue` against session `019dbaae-361e-78b0-a7e2-13d94df6f0ea` advanced to `phase=initial-implement`, emitted one chunk of stdout (first few seed fixtures being read) at 15:38:47Z, and then went silent. `status.json` `lastOutputAt` stayed at 15:38:47 while the codex process accumulated just ~1 second of CPU over the next 41 minutes — effectively idle, not actively reasoning. Per the 30-min \"hard-stall\" threshold in `operations/30-cli-operations.md` this needed intervention. Orchestrator killed the subprocess at 16:22Z. No envelope was written; the CLI reported \"completed exit 0\" only because my kill broke the pipe. Recovery: retry the same fix as a `quick-fix` (fresh codex, no reading-journey). Fix direction for CLI/adapter: surface a watchdog in the CLI itself that detects N-minute output silence and fails with a clear `PROVIDER_STALLED` code instead of hanging indefinitely. Alternatively, add a heartbeat line to the progress stream so orchestrators can distinguish \"codex is reasoning slowly\" from \"codex is wedged\". The continuation session handle (`019dbaae-...`) may or may not still be valid; safer to treat it as invalidated after a hard-kill and fall back to fresh implementor if retry fails. **Second instance:** 2026-04-23 18:07-18:51Z, Story 3 quick-fix 011 against the bundled empty-body + version-ID + perf-proof prompt. Started at 18:07:02, last output at 18:08:46 (1m44s in — codex had read files, run `git diff` inspecting the existing test shape, and was about to make edits), then silent for 43 min with ~2s codex CPU total. Same signature as first instance: started work cleanly, then wedged mid-session. Both instances were under `reasoning_effort: xhigh` (story-continue first, quick-fix second). Orchestrator killed at 18:51Z, retried as quick-fix 012. No watchdog timeout fired from the CLI side (`timeoutMs: 1800000` = 30 min configured) — the kernel didn't consider it \"dead\", codex wasn't crashing, it just stopped emitting stdout. Reinforces the watchdog-on-silence recommendation above. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:343:- Acceptance Rationale: 3 verify rounds (half of Story 2's 6 — new playbook working), final round `pass` with both verifiers clean. All 4 gates pass. Baseline +16 with no regressions. Real Mermaid render pipeline + server-side DOMPurify sanitization + client-side DOMPurify SVG sanitization + Mermaid directive strip + bounded per-diagram failures + unsupported-format fallback all landed per tech design.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:348:- Story Title: Story 2: Artifact Versions and Revision Review\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:379:  - (rd 4 + rd 5 carry) zero-version artifacts appear in `availableTargets`? → **accepted-risk / spec-tension**: Story 1 line 121+123 say zero-version = not a reviewable target (excluded from list); Story 2 AC-2.4 says workspace shows no-version state when reached. Interpretation: AC-2.4 is for deep-link navigation, not target-list discovery. Both server (line 259 test) and client (line 44 test) now correctly return the no-version state through direct URL. **Carrying to epic verification as a spec-clarification ask**: is AC-2.4's reachability meant to include process-surface entry? If yes, Story 1 line 123 should soften.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:546:- Story 2 rewrites Epic 3's checkpoint writer path to call `insertArtifactVersion` rather than overwriting\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-3-confirm.md:1:# Story 2 Verification — Sonnet B Round 3 Confirmation\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-3-confirm.md:42:`preparingEnvironmentProcessSurfaceFixture` at line 174 uses `status: 'running'`. This is not a traceability drift toward an impossible state — it is the settled post-hydration steady state (process is running while environment is being re-checked or rebuilt). The `preparing` environment state does occur with a `running` process in Story 3's controlled-execution context (environment rebuild during a running process). The fixture name makes this scenario legible. The pairing is semantically valid in the full epic model; it is not a Story 2 invariant violation (Story 2's invariant is that `running` cannot precede `ready` on the *initial* hydration path, which is enforced in service code, not in this fixture). Promoting to blocker would be a false positive.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-3-confirm.md:44:### Warning 2: `TC-2.6a/b/c` in `process-work-surface-page.test.ts` are outside Story 2's TC inventory\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review-round-3-confirm.md:48:The three tests (lines 1343, 1371, 1399) verify that the client work-surface page shows `State: Preparing environment` immediately after a Start or Resume action — without waiting for a WebSocket push. This is directly in scope of Story 2's AC-2.1 (start/resume enters visible preparation in the same session) and AC-2.3 (hydration progress visible live). The TC identifiers (`2.6a/b/c`) are outside the numbered AC/TC table in the story spec, but the behavior they cover is within the story boundary. This is a labeling gap, not a scope violation. The tests add defensive value and all pass. Promoting to blocker would reject correct coverage on a naming technicality. Flag for TC inventory update at Story 2 closeout if desired.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice5b-run.json:3:  \"result\": \"Done. Here's what changed:\\n\\n**`tests/fixtures/live-process.ts`** — added `environmentFailedUpsertLiveFixture` (seq 19, `failedEnvironmentFixture` — plain preparation failure, no checkpoint result).\\n\\n**`tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts`** — four Story 2 TCs are now explicit and semantically precise:\\n\\n| TC | Scenario | What changed |\\n|----|----------|-------------|\\n| TC-2.3a | hydration progress visible | No change (was already correct) |\\n| TC-2.3b | hydration failure visible | Now uses plain `failedEnvironmentFixture` (not checkpoint failure); asserts `state: 'failed'`, `blockedReason` contains \\\"Preparation failed\\\", `lastCheckpointResult: null` |\\n| TC-2.4a | running only after readiness | Now a three-step sequence: `preparing → ready → running` with intermediate state assertions |\\n| TC-2.4b | running doesn't appear after failed preparation | Now sequential `preparing → failed` using the plain failure fixture; explicitly asserts `state !== 'running'` |\\n\\n19/19 pass. Lint clean.\",\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice9-run.json:3:  \"result\": \"The slice is done. Here's what I found and verified:\\n\\n**What existed:** The full implementation was already in place from prior iterations — `environment/provider-adapter.ts`, `environment/process-environment.service.ts`, wiring in `app.ts`, env service injection in both start/resume services, and TC-2.3a/TC-2.3b in the live-updates test file.\\n\\n**What needed verification:** The initial test run showed a failing `S2-TC-2.1a` assertion — but reading the file confirmed it had already been updated to assert `ready` in the bootstrap (not `preparing`). The failing test shown in the initial run was from a stale cached run before the fix landed.\\n\\n**Final state:**\\n\\n| Suite | Result |\\n|-------|--------|\\n| `process-live-updates.test.ts` | 5/5 — 3 existing + TC-2.3a + TC-2.3b |\\n| `process-actions-api.test.ts` | 25/25 |\\n| Full `verify` | 220 tests, clean typecheck/lint/build |\\n\\n**The two new tests prove the server-driven path:**\\n- `TC-2.3a`: HTTP start → start response shows `preparing` → WebSocket receives `ready` upsert from background preparation\\n- `TC-2.3b`: HTTP start with `FailingProviderAdapter` → start response shows `preparing` → WebSocket receives `failed` upsert with the provider's error message as `blockedReason`\\n\\n**Design note for next slice:** `processEnvironmentService.executeHydration` passes `providerKind: null` to `upsertProcessEnvironmentState`. Fixing that to use a `providerKind` from the adapter is the natural first step of the provider-selection durability slice.\",\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-report-external-01.md:1:# Story 2 Implementation Report — External Worker 01\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-report-external-01.md:5:Deliver the first concrete Story 2 slice:\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-report-external-01.md:123:   Story 2's actual provider selection logic (Daytona vs local) is deferred until the provider\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-report-external-01.md:128:   the infrastructure from the full Story 2 execution slice (outside this slice's scope).\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-report-external-01.md:134:   environment state doesn't follow the full Story 2 flow for those paths yet.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice8-report.md:1:# Impl Slice 8 Report — Story 2 Execution Layer (preparing → ready | failed)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice5-run.json:3:  \"result\": \"All 19 tests pass. Summary of what changed in `process-live.test.ts`:\\n\\n**Renamed (no logic change):**\\n- `'applies environment upserts...'` → `TC-2.3a hydration progress becomes visible through environment live updates`\\n- `'preserves checkpoint-result visibility...'` → `TC-2.3b hydration failure becomes visible through environment live updates`\\n- Stripped incorrect `TC-2.3a/b` labels from history-ordering tests\\n- Stripped incorrect `TC-2.4a/b` labels from process-state transition tests\\n\\n**Added (2 new tests):**\\n- `TC-2.4a running begins after readiness` — state with `readyEnvironmentFixture`, applies `environmentRunningUpsertLiveFixture`, asserts `env.state === 'running'`\\n- `TC-2.4b running does not begin after failed preparation` — state with `preparingEnvironmentFixture`, applies `environmentCheckpointFailureUpsertLiveFixture`, asserts `env.state === 'failed'` with `blockedReason` set\\n\\nNo production code changes needed — existing implementation already handles all four paths.\",\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:1:# Story 2 Compliance Review\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:16:Secondary gaps (NONBLOCKING_WARNINGS): server-side live-publication tests for TC-2.3a/b are absent, TC-2.6* labels are undeclared in the story, and the WorkingSetPlan/HydrationPlan schema divergence accumulates technical debt for Story 3.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:82:**TC-2.3a — SATISFIED (client)**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:84:`TC-2.3a hydration progress becomes visible through environment live updates` in `process-live.test.ts` applies `environmentPreparingUpsertLiveFixture` and verifies the store's `environment.state` becomes `preparing`. The live reconciliation path (`applyLiveProcessMessage` with `entityType = 'environment'`) is tested and correct.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:86:**TC-2.3b — SATISFIED (client)**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:88:`TC-2.3b hydration failure becomes visible through environment live updates` applies `environmentFailedUpsertLiveFixture` and asserts `state: 'failed'`, `blockedReason: expect.stringContaining('Preparation failed')`, `lastCheckpointResult: null`. The fixture rename from `environmentCheckpointFailureUpsertLiveFixture` to `environmentFailedUpsertLiveFixture` is correct — a preparation failure has no checkpoint result.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:90:The tech-design-server Flow 2 and test plan both map TC-2.3a and TC-2.3b to `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts`. That file was not modified. The server-side path — where the orchestrator publishes `preparing` and later `failed` state to the live hub — is not tested. The existing Story 1 test proves `entityType: 'environment'` appears in the stream; it does not prove preparation or failure state transitions. This is a gap at the specified test layer. Coverage at the client layer is real and sufficient for story acceptance.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:154:| `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts` | TC-2.3a, TC-2.3b (server-side publication) | Existing Story 1 test confirms `environment` entity in stream. Preparing/failed state transitions from the server's publication path are untested at this layer. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:170:Four prior tests in `process-live.test.ts` had `TC-2.3a`, `TC-2.3b`, `TC-2.4a`, `TC-2.4b` labels that did not correspond to Story 2 conditions. These were renamed to plain descriptive names. This prevents false compliance claims from prior stories.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:183:Story 2 does not add `FakeProviderAdapter`. The test plan mentions `tests/utils/fake-provider-adapter.ts` as a planned utility. Its absence is correct given that no provider execution path exists. When Story 3 adds provider execution, the fake adapter will be needed.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:189:`auth-routes.test.ts` and `processes-api.test.ts` maintain local hand-rolled mock classes. Story 2 adds stub implementations for the three new PlatformStore methods. Stubs are plausible (null plan, pass-through upsert) and do not affect these tests' actual coverage targets.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:202:TC-2.3a and TC-2.3b are mapped to `process-live-updates.test.ts` by both tech-design-server and the test plan. The file was not extended. The publication path (start/resume service → live hub → websocket) exists and the story-1 snapshot test proves `environment` entity appears in the stream. But no test proves that `preparing` and `failed` states are published at the correct lifecycle moments.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:211:`CurrentProcessMaterialRefs` has no `outputIds`. The plan cannot include outputs even though the story's AC-2.2 lists them. The material refs interface predates Story 2 and was not extended here.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:225:- **Option A — Scope adjustment:** Update the story's AC-2.2 language and DefOD to read \"builds a hydration plan from current materials\" rather than \"hydrates...into the working copy.\" Update TC-2.2a/b to assert plan content only. Accept Story 2.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:234:**W-1: TC-2.3a/b server-side publication gap.**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:287:- `process-live-updates.test.ts` uses a `waitFor` polling loop with a 1500ms timeout for websocket tests. This is a pre-existing pattern, not introduced here. Not worth flagging in a Story 2 review.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/sonnet-review.md:289:- `process-work-surface-page.test.ts` TC-2.1a/b previously asserted \"Running\" as the visible body text after a start/resume. The Story 2 implementation correctly changes this to \"State: Preparing environment\" because the surface now shows preparation state, not running state. This is a behaviour change with real UX consequence that was handled correctly in both the implementation and the test update.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:301:- **TC-2.3a: Prior version opens distinctly**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:305:- **TC-2.3b: Versions remain ordered newest to oldest**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:978:### Story 2: Artifact Versions and Revision Review\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:994:**Prerequisite:** Story 2\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:932:| TC-2.3a | prior version opens distinctly | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts` | two versions; query prior | selectedVersionId ≠ currentVersionId |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:933:| TC-2.3b | versions ordered newest to oldest | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts` | three versions | versions[].createdAt descending |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:259:| TC-2.3a | `TC-2.3a prior version opens distinctly` | Two versions; query prior | GET artifact review | selectedVersionId ≠ currentVersionId |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:260:| TC-2.3b | `TC-2.3b versions ordered newest to oldest` | Three versions with distinct createdAt | GET artifact review | versions[] sorted descending by createdAt |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:394:| TC-2.3a | `TC-2.3a selecting prior version updates target` | Two-version list | Click prior version | new versionId becomes selection; body refreshes |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:395:| TC-2.3b | `TC-2.3b versions rendered newest to oldest` | Three versions with distinct createdAt | Mount switcher | DOM order descending |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation/impl-slice4b-report.md:1:# Slice 4b Report — Story 2: TC-2.1a/b Assertion Cleanup\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coherence-review.md:43:- **Story 2** owns durable artifact-version history, current-versus-prior revision visibility, version ordering, and the no-version state.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coherence-review.md:61:- Story 2 carries artifact review endpoint, artifact version, and selected-version identity contracts.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coherence-review.md:77:- **Epic 5 artifact-model alignment:** any earlier Epic 4 wording that implied a single primary process owner on an artifact is superseded. Story 1 reviewability is now process-reference / pinned-context based, and Story 2 version review is explicitly project-artifact + version-provenance based.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coherence-review.md:78:- **AC-2.4 zero-version reachability:** zero-version artifacts are not reviewable targets and are excluded from available target lists by Story 1. Story 2 AC-2.4 / TC-2.4a covers only the direct artifact URL case where an artifact identity is reached through an otherwise valid process review context despite having no durable versions. This resolves the apparent tension without changing reviewability rules.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coherence-review.md:95:- Story 2 owns version-switch performance, keyboard-reachable version selection, and readable artifact/version identity\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:190:Client state extends the existing `AppState` with a new `reviewWorkspace` slice, disjoint from `projectShell` and `processSurface`. The review workspace is not a second live surface; there is no WebSocket subscription for it in Epic 4. Bootstrap is a single HTTP fetch against the review endpoint, and reopen replays the same bootstrap against durable state.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:35:- Artifact version-history interaction owned by Story 2\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coverage.md:17:| AC-2.1 | TC-2.1a, TC-2.1b | Story 2 | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/artifact-review-panel.test.ts` | User-deliverable in Epic 4 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coverage.md:18:| AC-2.2 | TC-2.2a, TC-2.2b | Story 2 | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/artifact-review-panel.test.ts` | User-deliverable in Epic 4 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coverage.md:19:| AC-2.3 | TC-2.3a, TC-2.3b | Story 2 | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/version-switcher.test.ts` | User-deliverable in Epic 4 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coverage.md:20:| AC-2.4 | TC-2.4a | Story 2 | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/artifact-review-panel.test.ts` | Direct artifact URL only, through a valid process review context; zero-version artifacts remain excluded from target lists by Story 1 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coverage.md:42:| Switching between already-known versions updates within 1 second | Story 2 | `tests/service/client/version-switcher.test.ts` | Captured in Story 2 Technical Design and Definition of Done |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coverage.md:51:| Review navigation, version selection, and export actions are keyboard reachable | Story 1, Story 2, Story 5 | `tests/service/client/a11y.test.ts` | Each story owns keyboard reachability for its control surface |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coverage.md:52:| Artifact identity, version identity, and review-target status are readable text, not color alone | Story 1, Story 2, Story 6 | `tests/service/client/a11y.test.ts` | Entry, version review, and unavailable/degraded states keep text-visible identity and status |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coverage.md:64:| Path 1.3 | Review the current and prior durable versions of one artifact | Story 2 | TC-2.1a, TC-2.1b, TC-2.2a, TC-2.2b, TC-2.3a, TC-2.3b | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/artifact-review-panel.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/version-switcher.test.ts` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coverage.md:65:| Path 1.4 | Reach a zero-version artifact only by direct artifact URL inside a valid process review context and show the no-version state | Story 2 | TC-2.4a | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/artifact-review-panel.test.ts` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/01-review-entry-and-workspace-bootstrap.md:130:- An artifact with no durable version and a package with no durable members are not reviewable targets. Direct-URL access to a zero-version artifact identity inside an otherwise valid process review context is handled by Story 2 AC-2.4 as a no-version target state, not as target-list discovery. A pathologically zero-member package snapshot is treated as unavailable, not as an empty target state.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/03-markdown-and-mermaid-review.md:38:- Story 2 artifact versions and revision review\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/03-markdown-and-mermaid-review.md:75:This story consumes the selected artifact version from Story 2 and turns it into readable markdown with bounded render failures.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/02-artifact-versions-and-revision-review.md:1:# Story 2: Artifact Versions and Revision Review\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/02-artifact-versions-and-revision-review.md:70:- **TC-2.3a: Prior version opens distinctly**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/02-artifact-versions-and-revision-review.md:74:- **TC-2.3b: Versions remain ordered newest to oldest**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/02-artifact-versions-and-revision-review.md:86:Empty-state note: Story 2 is the only place that uses the review-target\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/02-artifact-versions-and-revision-review.md:101:Story 2 is version-aware, not owner-aware. A later process may review or revise\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/02-artifact-versions-and-revision-review.md:155:Story 2 depends on the version identity fields and ordering rules in this shape. Story 3 exercises `contentKind`, `bodyStatus`, `body`, `bodyError`, and `mermaidBlocks` as rendered review behavior.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/02-artifact-versions-and-revision-review.md:175:Bootstrap-specific note: Story 2's dedicated artifact endpoint may still return\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/02-artifact-versions-and-revision-review.md:193:- Story tests cover TC-2.1a through TC-2.1b, TC-2.2a through TC-2.2b, TC-2.3a through TC-2.3b, and TC-2.4a\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
