ss\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:155:- **TC-1.3a: Current process materials show referenced artifact**\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:159:- **TC-1.3b: Unrelated process does not gain automatic current-material\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:177:5. System updates project artifact summaries and process current-material reads\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:182:**AC-2.1:** When a process revises an existing project artifact, the system\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:356:- **TC-4.2b: Unrelated project artifact version not in current package-building\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:398:version may become unavailable while other project artifacts remain healthy. The\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:443:   availability accurately rather than implying a primary-process ownership\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:604:2. Which existing artifact summary fields should be removed versus preserved as\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:627:**Delivers:** Processes can reference existing project artifacts and new\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:628:process-created artifacts automatically join the project artifact set without\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:632:- AC-1.1\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:633:- AC-1.2\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:634:- AC-1.3\\\\ntests/service/client/process-router.test.ts:150:  it('TC-1.1a opening a process from the project shell navigates to the dedicated process route', async () => {\\\\ntests/service/client/process-router.test.ts:172:  it('TC-1.1b direct process URL mounts the process work surface', async () => {\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/04-cross-process-package-alignment.md:62:- **TC-4.2b: Unrelated project artifact version not in current package-building context is blocked**\\\\nconvex/processEnvironmentStates.ts:313:        artifactIds: state?.currentArtifactIds ?? [],\\\\nconvex/processEnvironmentStates.ts:323:        artifactIds: state?.currentArtifactIds ?? [],\\\\nconvex/processEnvironmentStates.ts:333:        artifactIds: state?.currentArtifactIds ?? [],\\\\ntests/service/client/source-attachment-section.test.ts:39:      `Attached to ${processScopedSourceFixture.processDisplayLabel}.`,\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/05-reopen-and-degraded-provenance-states.md:38:- Story 1 project artifact association without process ownership\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/05-reopen-and-degraded-provenance-states.md:69:**AC-5.3:** Unavailable or degraded review states describe reference or version availability accurately rather than implying a primary-process ownership failure.\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/01-project-artifact-association-without-process-ownership.md:5:Make project artifacts project-scoped durable assets, keep process-local visibility in current materials, and remove single-process ownership language from project-shell artifact state.\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/01-project-artifact-association-without-process-ownership.md:24:- Project-shell artifact summary no longer implies primary process ownersh